.Dd $Mdocdate: October 23 2026 $
.Dt SIGNET-TEMPLATE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm signet-template
.Nd signet HTML template files
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr signet 1
renders its pages from files in the directory named by
.Va templates_dir
in
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5 ,
by default
.Pa /etc/signet/templates
on
.Ox
and
.Pa /var/www/signet/templates
in the packaged configuration.
.Pp
Templates are parsed once at startup with the semantics of Go's
.Li html/template
package: all files matching
.Pa *.html
in that directory are loaded, and their contents are HTML-escaped where they
appear as values.
Changes on disk are picked up on the next start of the service.
.Pp
The directory shipped with the package is
.Pa /usr/local/share/examples/signet/web/templates ;
the service copies it into the runtime directory on first start, after which
the runtime copy is the one that is used and may be edited freely.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa login.html
The login page, served for
.Cm GET /login .
.It Pa webauthn.html
The security-key page at
.Pa /webauthn/keys .
It receives no variables: its script calls
.Pa /webauthn/credentials
and reads any invite from the URL fragment.
.It Pa recover.html
The password recovery page, served for
.Cm GET /recover .
.It Pa register.html
The registration page, served for
.Cm GET /register .
.It Pa account.html
The account page, served for
.Cm GET /account
to a signed-in user.
It receives
.Va .Email ,
.Va .Fresh ,
which says whether the sign-in is recent enough to change anything,
.Va .PasswordEnabled ,
.Va .HasPassword ,
.Va .WebAuthnEnabled ,
.Va .RadiusAccount ,
true for an account whose password is a RADIUS server's, which has neither a
password nor keys here,
.Va .TOTPEnabled ,
.Va .TOTPKeys ,
each with
.Va .ID ,
.Va .Label
and
.Va .CreatedAt ,
.Va .RecoveryLeft ,
.Va .MaxTOTPKeys ,
.Va .AvatarsEnabled ,
.Va .Avatar ,
the path of the account's picture or empty,
.Va .Identicon ,
a pattern drawn from the address as a
.Li data\&:
URL, shown when there is no picture, and
.Va .AvatarSize .
.It Pa email/account-change.html , email/account-change.txt
The notice sent when an account changes.
It receives
.Va .Email ,
.Va .Change ,
which says what happened, and
.Va .AppName .
.It Pa email/pin.html , email/pin.txt
The HTML and plain-text bodies of the email PIN message.
They are separate from the page templates and use their own variable set.
.It Pa email/recover.html , email/recover.txt
The message with a recovery link.
.It Pa email/password-changed.html , email/password-changed.txt
The notice sent after a recovery link changes a password.
.It Pa email/register.html , email/register.txt
The message with a registration link.
.It Pa email/account-exists.html , email/account-exists.txt
The notice sent when someone tries to register an address that has an account.
.El
.Sh PAGE TEMPLATES
A page template may be written in either of two styles.
Either it is a standalone document named after its file
.Pq Pa login.html ,
or it wraps the markup in a named definition:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{{define "login"}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
\&...
{{end}}
.Ed
.Pp
Both work.
When the definition exists it is preferred, because
.Li html/template
registers the file name as an empty wrapper in that case.
.Ss Paths
Every page template may call
.Li basePath ,
which gives the instance's
.Va base_path
.Po see
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5
.Pc :
empty at the root, else like
.Dq /comments-auth .
Write each address of this instance with it, so the page works under a base:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<form method="POST" action="{{basePath}}/login">
<script src="{{basePath}}/static/js/webauthn.js"
        data-base-path="{{basePath}}"></script>
<script>const signetBase = {{basePath}};</script>
.Ed
.Pp
Inside a script it gives a quoted string.
.Pa webauthn.js
reads the base from its tag's
.Li data-base-path ,
and calls the server there.
A page edited before 0.13.25 names its addresses from the root, which is still
right for an instance without a base.
.Sh LOGIN TEMPLATE VARIABLES
The following fields are available inside
.Pa login.html :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va .AllowRegistration
Boolean.
True when
.Va self_registration
is
.Dq enabled
in the configuration.
.It Va .PasswordEnabled
Boolean.
True when password authentication is available.
.It Va .WebAuthnEnabled
Boolean.
True when WebAuthn is configured and its service started.
.It Va .EmailPINEnabled
Boolean.
True when the email PIN method is available.
.It Va .TOTPEnabled
Boolean.
True when
.Va auth_methods.totp
is enabled.
.It Va .RadiusEnabled
Boolean.
True when
.Va radius.enabled
is, and a name that is not a mail address may sign in by password.
The shipped template then asks for an
.Dq email address or user name
in a text field, since a browser refuses a plain name in an
.Li email
field.
.It Va .Pending
The token of the second step of a sign-in, or the empty string.
The shipped template then shows a form posting it with
.Li code ,
or with
.Li action ,
to
.Cm /login ,
and an edited one must keep those forms and the script that shows them,
or accounts with
TOTP, and every account while
.Va second_factor
is
.Dq required ,
cannot sign in.
.It Va .Step
Which second step the page is at, or the empty string:
.Dq code
for a code from an authenticator app,
.Dq mail
for a PIN mailed after a password,
.Dq radius
for the answer to a RADIUS server's challenge, posted as
.Li code ,
with the server's prompt in
.Va .Message ,
or
.Dq enrol
for adding a second factor.
.It Va .EnrolTOTP , .EnrolKey
Booleans, at the
.Dq enrol
step: whether an authenticator app, or a security key, may be added.
An app is added by posting
.Li action=totp-begin ,
then
.Li action=totp-finish
with a
.Li code ;
a key by posting
.Li action=key ,
which answers
.Sy 303
to the key page with a one-time invite.
.It Va .TOTPStarted , .TOTPSecret , .TOTPQR
After
.Li totp-begin :
true, the app's key to type in, and a QR code holding it, as a
.Li data\&:
URI made by the server.
.It Va .RecoveryCodes , .Continue
After an app is added: its recovery codes, shown only this once, and where the
sign-in returns to.
The session is already set.
.It Va .Error
A message to show in the error banner, or the empty string.
.It Va .Message
A message to show in the success banner, or the empty string.
.It Va .Referrer
The return location taken from
.Cm ?referrer=
.Pq whole, when a web server sent it unencoded ,
or from the page that linked to the login form, or the empty string.
It is normally placed in a hidden field so the redirect survives the POST:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<input type="hidden" name="referrer" value="{{.Referrer}}">
.Ed
.El
.Pp
The method flags let one template serve every installation; sections are
switched off when their method is unavailable:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{{if .PasswordEnabled}}
<form id="login-form"> ... </form>
{{end}}
{{if and .PasswordEnabled (or .WebAuthnEnabled .EmailPINEnabled)}}
<div class="divider">or</div>
{{end}}
{{if .WebAuthnEnabled}}
<button id="webauthn-button">Sign in with Security Key</button>
{{end}}
.Ed
.Pp
Unknown fields render as the empty string, so a template that references a
variable this version does not provide fails silently rather than with an
error.
.Sh RETURN LOCATION
After a successful login the browser is sent to a return location.
The first usable value wins:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
the
.Va referrer
field posted with the form
.Pq the hidden input above ;
.It
the
.Cm ?referrer=
query parameter;
.It
the HTTP
.Ev Referer
header, including a
.Cm ?referrer=
it carries;
.It
the account page,
.Pa /account
under
.Va base_path .
.El
.Pp
Only local paths
.Pq e.g. Pa /dashboard
and absolute URLs on the same host are honoured; anything else falls back to
the account page, so the parameter cannot be used to redirect users to another
site.
This instance's
.Pa /login ,
.Pa /register ,
.Pa /recover
and
.Pa /logout
never count, and the login page's
.Va .Referrer
is empty rather than one of them.
.Sh RECOVER TEMPLATE VARIABLES
The following fields are available inside
.Pa recover.html :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va .RecoveryEnabled
Boolean.
True when
.Va password_recovery
is
.Dq enabled ;
when false the shipped template hides the form and explains why.
.It Va .Error
A message to show in an error banner, or the empty string.
.It Va .Message
An informational message, or the empty string.
.It Va .Email
The address that was submitted, so the form can be re-filled.
.It Va .Token
The token of a live link when a password was refused, so the form can be sent
again, or the empty string.
.It Va .Done
Boolean.
True once the password has been changed.
.El
.Pp
A link carries its token in the URL fragment, so the page's script must read it,
remove it from the address bar and check it with
.Cm POST /recover
before asking for a password.
An edited template has to keep that script: see the shipped one.
.Sh REGISTER TEMPLATE VARIABLES
.Pa register.html
receives
.Va .RegistrationEnabled ,
.Va .VerificationRequired ,
which says whether the form takes only an address,
.Va .Error ,
.Va .Message ,
.Va .Email ,
.Va .Token
and
.Va .Done ,
which mean what they do in
.Pa recover.html ,
and it needs the same script.
.Sh LINK MESSAGE TEMPLATE VARIABLES
The following fields are available inside
.Pa email/recover.* ,
.Pa email/password-changed.* ,
.Pa email/register.*
and
.Pa email/account-exists.* :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va .Link
The recovery or registration link, or the sign-in page in
.Pa account-exists ;
empty in
.Pa password-changed .
.It Va .Email
The account's address.
.It Va .Lifetime
How long the link works, in words, such as
.Dq 1 hour ;
empty in the notices.
.It Va .AppName
The application name.
.El
.Pp
Without a text template a built-in text is used,
and without an HTML template the
message has no HTML part.
.Sh EMAIL PIN TEMPLATE VARIABLES
The following fields are available inside both
.Pa email/pin.html
and
.Pa email/pin.txt :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va .PIN
The six-digit PIN.
.It Va .Email
The address the message is sent to.
.It Va .ExpiryMinutes
Lifetime of the PIN in minutes
.Pq default 10 .
.It Va .AppName
Name of the application, for use in the greeting or signature.
.El
.Pp
The message is sent as plain text from
.Pa email/pin.txt ,
or a built-in body if that is missing.
If
.Pa email/pin.html
exists, it is added as the HTML alternative.
A template that fails to parse stops the message from being sent,
and the failure
is logged.
.Sh APPEARANCE
The shipped
.Pa login.html
contains both a light and a dark palette.
Light is the default: the dark colours apply only inside
.Bd -literal -offset indent
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { ... }
.Ed
.Pp
so a browser that has not expressed a preference
.Pq or reports "light"
keeps the light theme.
All colours are CSS custom properties declared on
.Li :root ,
so a local template may override any of them, for example to match the
surrounding site:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
:root { --primary: #0a7d32; }
.Ed
.Pp
The variables are
.Va --bg ,
.Va --surface ,
.Va --text ,
.Va --heading ,
.Va --label ,
.Va --muted ,
.Va --faint ,
.Va --border ,
.Va --input-bg ,
.Va --primary ,
.Va --primary-hover ,
.Va --primary-disabled ,
.Va --secondary ,
.Va --secondary-hover ,
.Va --secondary-disabled ,
.Va --error-bg ,
.Va --error-fg ,
.Va --error-border ,
.Va --success-bg ,
.Va --success-fg ,
.Va --success-border ,
.Va --shadow
and
.Va --focus-ring .
.Sh EXAMPLES
A minimal standalone login page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>Sign in</title></head>
<body>
<form method="POST" action="/login">
  <input type="email" name="email" required>
  <input type="password" name="password" required>
  <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
</form>
</body>
</html>
.Ed
.Pp
This form posts without JavaScript and is answered with a redirect and a
session cookie.
The packaged page instead submits with the JavaScript
.Li fetch()
API and expects a JSON reply.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr signet 1 ,
.Xr signet-config.yaml 5 ,
.Xr signet-hooks 5
.Sh CAVEATS
Templates are parsed at startup, and
.Dv SIGHUP
does not reload them.
After editing a template, restart the service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
doas rcctl restart signet
.Ed
.Pp
The page templates are the local customization point: a package upgrade does
not overwrite an existing template directory.
Compare the packaged examples before upgrading if the variables above change,
and copy new pages such as
.Pa webauthn.html
yourself.
